 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-spc-001"></a>
+
+Staff also ask the inverse of the veterinarian directory's question: which veterinarians hold a given specialty. The clinic therefore publishes a specialty directory naming every specialty it knows, under its stored name, with the veterinarians holding each `[REQ-SPC-001]`. Each veterinarian appears by full name — first name, then last name. A veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere on the page, which lists specialties rather than the roster. Every specialty appears on one page, with no paging. The page is reached at an address of its own, and nothing links to it; a visible entry point is deferred. The directory only reads: NG-2 stands, so neither veterinarians nor specialties can be managed from it. Wording the page introduces falls under `REQ-LANG-002`, as on every other page.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-SPC-001]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every one of them is listed under its stored name.
+- `[REQ-SPC-001]` given a specialty one or more veterinarians hold, when the directory is opened, then each of those veterinarians is shown by first name then last name.
+- `[REQ-SPC-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on the page.
+- `[REQ-SPC-001]` given every specialty the clinic knows, when the directory is opened, then all of them appear on one page and no paging is offered.
+- `[REQ-SPC-001]` given a reader who opens the directory's address directly, when the request is made, then the page is returned.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty no veterinarian holds is still listed, with no veterinarian shown under it.
+2. A veterinarian holding more than one specialty appears once under each specialty they hold.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
